TASK 1: gettweetbydate.sh
- Purpose: Accepts a date parameter (format YY-MM-DD or YYYY-MM-DD), ensures the directory ~/TWEETS exists, and outputs all tweets that occurred on that date from the datasets into ~/TWEETS/<date>.out.
- Script Content:
    #!/bin/bash
    if [ -z "$1" ]; then
        echo "Usage: $0 <YY-MM-DD or YYYY-MM-DD>"
        exit 1
    fi

    DATE="$1"
    mkdir -p ~/TWEETS

    # Greps tweets matching the date (supports both YY-MM-DD and YYYY-MM-DD)
    grep -E "($DATE|20$DATE)" /mnt/scratch/CS131_billa/billandreopoulos/CS131_wba/DATA/downloaded_tweets_extend*.tsv > ~/TWEETS/"$DATE".out
